WEBVTT

00:01.820 --> 00:05.720
His Most August Majesty's kingdom of Ozmargo

00:05.720 --> 00:10.220
consists of 32 key cities 
and 15 vassal states.

00:10.520 --> 00:14.700
The capital of Karanbul, where 
this palace stands, is its heart.

00:15.080 --> 00:19.880
Beasts of many species gather from far 
and wide, fostering a rich culture of...

00:21.390 --> 00:23.170
Are you listening?!

00:23.170 --> 00:26.220
H-Huh? What part were we reading, again?

00:26.220 --> 00:27.950
Sari!

00:27.950 --> 00:31.850
We managed to translate these 
books into human writing.

00:31.850 --> 00:32.790
Writing.

00:33.130 --> 00:35.930
Thank you, Cy, Clops.

00:38.160 --> 00:42.100
But why did you start 
studying out of the blue?

00:42.100 --> 00:48.140
Since I came here as a sacrifice, I don't 
know the first thing about this kingdom.

00:49.170 --> 00:51.810
So I decided to learn,

00:52.280 --> 00:55.330
but it's too much for me 
to take in all at once.

00:56.710 --> 01:02.380
No mere human could appreciate 
the lofty history of beastkind.

01:02.380 --> 01:05.740
I reluctantly consented to teach you 
because His Majesty ordered it,

01:05.740 --> 01:07.700
but going further would be a waste of time.

01:07.700 --> 01:09.540
I will return to my duties.

01:10.190 --> 01:12.320
What are your duties, Mr. Chancellor?

01:12.320 --> 01:14.320
The same as any chancellor!

01:14.320 --> 01:19.480
I assist the king in affairs of state, 
of which he has many to manage.

01:19.800 --> 01:22.780
He hasn't been able to rest in far too long.

02:55.020 --> 03:00.030
Beasts and a Human Town

03:00.790 --> 03:01.990
What?

03:02.370 --> 03:06.020
I'd like to go outside the 
palace with you. Can't we?

03:06.730 --> 03:11.800
Do <i>you</i> seriously believe I would permit it?

03:11.800 --> 03:15.250
I'd like to see how normal beasts live.

03:15.250 --> 03:20.110
No. I supply all your wants in the palace.

03:20.110 --> 03:22.070
There's no need.

03:22.070 --> 03:23.420
Are you sure, sire?

03:23.740 --> 03:28.710
Still, I think you need a 
break every now and then.

03:31.810 --> 03:33.360
Pretty please?

03:35.910 --> 03:37.970
Once you start pestering, you never stop.

03:37.970 --> 03:38.580
Very we—

03:38.580 --> 03:42.070
Yay! Thank you, sire! I love you!

03:42.930 --> 03:44.900
But only on one condition.

03:50.220 --> 03:53.940
Oh, wow! It's so crowded!

03:53.940 --> 03:57.500
And there really are all 
kinds of people here.

03:57.940 --> 04:01.310
This is a major street in 
the heart of the capital.

04:01.310 --> 04:03.480
Traffic is especially heavy here.

04:05.550 --> 04:07.520
Hm? What's so amusing?

04:07.520 --> 04:10.100
I-It's just that...

04:10.480 --> 04:12.750
you look so suspicious, sire!

04:12.750 --> 04:14.310
I can't help that.

04:14.310 --> 04:17.030
More importantly, remember your promise.

04:17.350 --> 04:21.440
I won't cause trouble, 
and I'll be home before dark.

04:21.650 --> 04:25.730
<i>Unacceptable! Unacceptable! 
You mustn't do that, sire!</i>

04:21.670 --> 04:26.080
I sent Anubis to a neighboring town. 
We must return before him,

04:25.730 --> 04:28.300
<i>You mustn't do that, either! Nor this!</i>

04:26.080 --> 04:28.940
or I'll be forced to hear 
more of his griping.

04:28.300 --> 04:31.460
<i>Do you understand your own position, sire?!</i>

04:29.300 --> 04:32.820
Even <i>you're</i> afraid of his lectures.

04:31.460 --> 04:32.820
<i>Unacceptable!</i>

04:33.250 --> 04:35.300
Okay, then. Let's get going, sire!

04:35.540 --> 04:36.780
Also,

04:37.460 --> 04:39.850
stop addressing me as "sire."

04:40.420 --> 04:41.750
Oh, that's right.

04:42.440 --> 04:43.570
In that case...

04:44.690 --> 04:46.080
Let's go, Leo!

04:47.340 --> 04:50.920
This fine cloth was dyed 
by Granian craftsmen.

04:50.920 --> 04:53.520
You'll never find this color again.

04:53.520 --> 04:55.310
My, what lovely gemstones.

04:55.310 --> 04:59.980
You have a good eye. 
What would you say to this piece?

05:02.080 --> 05:06.570
Oh, pardon me, miss. My, how little you are.

05:08.040 --> 05:09.970
<i>It's so lively.</i>

05:09.970 --> 05:14.490
<i>But when I see it like this, it's not 
much different from a human town.</i>

05:16.190 --> 05:19.450
Hm? Something smells nice.

05:19.450 --> 05:21.440
Oh, a bakery!

05:22.270 --> 05:25.420
Welcome, miss. It's fresh out of the oven.

05:25.420 --> 05:26.770
So's this.

05:27.080 --> 05:29.590
So they have bread here, too.

05:29.590 --> 05:33.010
They didn't serve it in the 
palace, so I never knew.

05:33.270 --> 05:34.460
The palace?

05:34.460 --> 05:36.760
Did you two come from the palace?

05:37.970 --> 05:40.940
You've got great horns. Like the king.

05:42.140 --> 05:47.270
Come, now, His Majesty would never 
dress up like such a shady character.

05:47.270 --> 05:52.630
Word to the wise, they say the king 
hates anything made from wheat.

05:52.630 --> 05:55.130
Although it's a luxury in these parts.

05:56.580 --> 06:02.670
Under the last king, royals and aristocrats 
snapped up all the rarities.

06:02.950 --> 06:07.740
But the current king couldn't care less 
about delicacies or fancy decorations.

06:07.740 --> 06:10.700
That's why we're in business.

06:10.700 --> 06:11.550
Indeed.

06:11.780 --> 06:16.810
These days, big-shot nobles 
come into the city to shop,

06:16.810 --> 06:18.770
so his tastes are great for us.

06:24.720 --> 06:27.100
Here, Leo. This is yours.

06:27.100 --> 06:31.150
I don't need it. Those spongy 
things won't satisfy my hunger.

06:31.150 --> 06:34.090
Really? Are you <i>sure</i> you don't want it?

06:34.530 --> 06:39.420
I'm full right now, so I'd love 
it if you ate one for me.

06:39.420 --> 06:42.910
What fool buys food on a full stomach?

06:43.370 --> 06:45.940
I'm sorry, but...

06:45.940 --> 06:49.600
Come on. Say "ahh." Please?

06:49.600 --> 06:51.330
"Ahh."

06:53.650 --> 06:54.520
Well?

06:55.220 --> 06:59.810
It's like chewing on air, but... 
well, it's not bad.

07:00.970 --> 07:02.410
I'm so glad!

07:05.840 --> 07:06.980
What's wrong?

07:07.420 --> 07:10.780
Mommy's gone. Mommy's gone.

07:10.780 --> 07:12.440
You got separated from your mommy?

07:12.440 --> 07:13.110
Yeah.

07:13.760 --> 07:14.910
What's your name?

07:14.910 --> 07:16.280
Bolas.

07:16.720 --> 07:20.310
Okay, Bolas. Let's find your mommy together.

07:20.310 --> 07:23.740
The sun is soon to set. 
We must return to the castle.

07:24.420 --> 07:28.950
I know. We need to find 
her quickly, or we'll be late.

07:31.400 --> 07:35.630
Bolas's mom, are you there?

07:35.630 --> 07:38.100
Bolas's mom!

07:38.100 --> 07:39.680
Bolas's mo—

07:40.640 --> 07:43.020
Wh-What?

07:43.850 --> 07:47.490
Give the child here. 
The mother can see it this way.

07:48.120 --> 07:50.610
Yes. Thank you, Leo.

07:50.610 --> 07:52.600
We'll find her, then hurry back.

07:54.260 --> 07:56.570
<i>Why did I feel dizzy just now?</i>

07:56.570 --> 07:58.670
<i>Is it from carrying this heavy head around?</i>

07:59.250 --> 08:03.050
Mommy's gone. I can't find her.

08:05.510 --> 08:07.930
Sorry, Leo. Would you bend down a bit?

08:11.010 --> 08:13.730
It's all right. We'll find her.

08:14.150 --> 08:15.930
So don't cry,

08:16.290 --> 08:16.990
okay?

08:19.120 --> 08:20.130
Okay.

08:24.780 --> 08:26.230
Bolas!

08:26.610 --> 08:27.850
Mommy!

08:27.850 --> 08:30.490
Where have you been?! I was looking for you!

08:30.490 --> 08:32.080
I'm so glad you're all right.

08:32.980 --> 08:35.050
Thank you so much.

08:35.050 --> 08:37.340
No, we didn't do anything...

08:38.360 --> 08:39.190
Watch out!

08:42.090 --> 08:43.460
A h-human!

08:43.460 --> 08:44.450
A human?!

08:44.450 --> 08:45.330
Did she say "human"?!

08:46.750 --> 08:49.010
I'm fine, Leo. So is the child.

08:49.010 --> 08:50.210
Bolas!

08:50.210 --> 08:51.300
Here, ma'a—

08:51.300 --> 08:53.390
Don't touch my child!

08:55.100 --> 08:57.730
She was in our shop earlier.

08:57.730 --> 08:59.410
Did she steal anything?

08:59.410 --> 09:01.160
Someone, call the guards!

09:01.160 --> 09:02.810
Get out of our land!

09:02.810 --> 09:04.350
Filthy human!

09:14.130 --> 09:16.170
Look! The human's gone!

09:16.170 --> 09:19.190
Find her! She can't have gone far!

09:20.880 --> 09:25.180
We're going home before 
this uproar gets any worse.

09:25.180 --> 09:25.980
Okay.

09:30.850 --> 09:33.970
Your Majesty, where in 
the world have you been?

09:34.490 --> 09:38.470
A human was reportedly spotted in the city.

09:38.470 --> 09:40.180
Let us talk of this later.

09:40.180 --> 09:41.750
Oh, Your Majesty!

09:41.750 --> 09:44.450
These documents require your seal at once.

09:44.450 --> 09:46.000
Later, I said!

09:47.100 --> 09:49.900
I'm so sorry, sire!

09:51.870 --> 09:54.210
I ended up causing trouble.

09:54.620 --> 09:59.300
I got careless, and I scared 
all the townspeople.

09:59.300 --> 10:03.760
You think those beasts feared a human?

10:03.760 --> 10:06.240
Yes. I mean...

10:06.900 --> 10:09.360
The way they looked at me

10:10.230 --> 10:14.000
was just how humans look 
when they talk about beasts.

10:15.430 --> 10:19.250
It must be because they have 
a history of war with us.

10:20.530 --> 10:25.210
Beasts may be a lot 
stronger than humans are,

10:26.130 --> 10:32.550
but no one I met today seemed 
like they <i>wanted</i> to fight humans.

10:33.050 --> 10:36.570
And we humans are the same way.

10:37.530 --> 10:39.680
Both beasts and humans

10:39.680 --> 10:41.900
seem alike in your eyes.

10:42.610 --> 10:47.110
I suppose your gaze can 
penetrate any deception.

10:47.880 --> 10:48.520
Huh?

10:49.280 --> 10:51.530
I should be the one to apologize.

10:52.310 --> 10:55.880
I exposed you to danger 
while we were together.

10:55.880 --> 10:57.360
It wasn't your fault.

10:58.000 --> 11:01.540
No, I let down my guard.

11:01.990 --> 11:08.910
I enjoyed this day of rest with you 
from the bottom of my heart.

11:09.550 --> 11:14.060
Since the day I was born a king, 
I've never before made such a blunder.

11:17.630 --> 11:22.800
You shouldn't bow to people, sire. 
The chancellor will scold you.

11:22.800 --> 11:23.960
And besides...

11:26.950 --> 11:33.050
It wasn't a blunder. I had tons of fun!

11:39.810 --> 11:40.890
Sariphi?!

11:42.130 --> 11:45.910
Then, this land's miasma is the cause?

11:45.910 --> 11:48.350
Is that your diagnosis, my lord priest?

11:48.350 --> 11:53.220
It is. All humans are 
susceptible to the miasma.

11:53.220 --> 11:58.010
And no human has ever dwelt 
in our lands so long.

11:58.260 --> 12:00.610
Meaning, if she stays...

12:00.610 --> 12:04.000
If she stays, it will erode her vitality

12:04.000 --> 12:06.960
until she ultimately expires.

12:07.950 --> 12:10.070
Are you in pain, Sariphi?

12:11.780 --> 12:15.790
Don't worry, sire. Go back to your work.

12:17.260 --> 12:19.270
I'll be fine.

12:20.310 --> 12:21.400
Sariphi.

12:22.110 --> 12:25.090
If you remain in my kingdom, you will...

12:26.230 --> 12:29.890
<i>No matter what, I have...</i>

12:31.460 --> 12:37.070
But I swear, I'll save you.

12:39.780 --> 12:43.130
The sky... It's blue.

12:45.440 --> 12:46.340
Oh!

12:47.280 --> 12:48.830
You're awake?

12:54.480 --> 12:56.160
You're awake?

12:56.630 --> 12:57.740
<i>A human?</i>

12:58.240 --> 13:00.770
Dear! Dear!

13:01.400 --> 13:03.160
Um... Where am I?

13:03.160 --> 13:06.210
My clinic, on the outskirts of Turis.

13:06.550 --> 13:09.790
You were brought here for miasma poisoning.

13:09.790 --> 13:13.350
Don't you remember? You must 
have come from the border.

13:13.350 --> 13:17.300
The wind blows miasma 
over to our side sometimes.

13:18.150 --> 13:20.540
<i>So this is human land?</i>

13:21.690 --> 13:24.250
Oh, don't get up yet.

13:24.250 --> 13:26.190
Take your medicine first.

13:26.530 --> 13:33.060
It's made from ambrosia, a fruit that grows 
only in lands with the purest of waters.

13:33.060 --> 13:36.680
It will purify the miasma 
inside you in no time.

13:36.910 --> 13:38.240
Medicine?

13:39.430 --> 13:41.890
But I have no money.

13:41.890 --> 13:45.300
Don't worry. We've already been paid.

13:46.830 --> 13:48.510
Three days ago now,

13:49.020 --> 13:53.260
someone left you unconscious 
in front of the clinic.

13:55.190 --> 13:56.600
<i>So I was left here.</i>

13:56.990 --> 13:59.430
We heard a knock in the night.

13:59.430 --> 14:03.310
By the time we got outside, 
they were already gone,

14:03.310 --> 14:08.810
but they left more than enough money 
for your treatment, as well as this note.

14:12.010 --> 14:16.890
<i>Beast writing and the royal seal? 
Is it from the king?</i>

14:17.280 --> 14:19.120
<i>I can't read it...</i>

14:20.480 --> 14:24.220
If you remain in my kingdom, you will...

14:24.530 --> 14:26.740
<i>...but I'm sure that's what it's about.</i>

14:27.480 --> 14:29.680
<i>The king...</i>

14:30.110 --> 14:31.680
<i>saved me.</i>

14:34.470 --> 14:36.420
Good day to you, Doctor.

14:36.420 --> 14:39.260
Why, hello, Roche.

14:39.260 --> 14:41.360
How have you been feeling since then?

14:41.660 --> 14:43.220
Better, thanks to you.

14:43.220 --> 14:47.280
But tell me, have you hired a new assistant?

14:47.280 --> 14:48.470
What?

14:48.470 --> 14:51.160
I haven't seen that girl 
in your yard before.

14:51.160 --> 14:53.410
Oh, her. She's...

14:53.880 --> 14:55.770
a patient, actually.

14:55.770 --> 14:57.170
A patient?

14:58.210 --> 14:59.500
Come on in!

14:59.500 --> 15:02.460
Oh, wait, they don't say that at clinics.

15:02.460 --> 15:04.180
Hello, sir.

15:05.950 --> 15:07.460
You sure seem healthy.

15:07.460 --> 15:11.260
Sariphi, you're not well yet.

15:11.260 --> 15:13.340
Don't force yourself to help out.

15:13.750 --> 15:15.000
I'm fine.

15:15.790 --> 15:20.010
But we got paid handsomely to cure you.

15:20.300 --> 15:23.330
Yes, but that money wasn't mine.

15:23.940 --> 15:26.170
<i>And when I stop moving,</i>

15:27.340 --> 15:28.870
<i>I can't help but start thinking.</i>

15:29.810 --> 15:31.740
Is there anything else you need done?

15:51.400 --> 15:55.360
Goodness, I'm lucky you're 
such a hard worker.

15:55.360 --> 15:57.780
The patients love you.

15:57.780 --> 15:59.020
I didn't do much.

15:59.020 --> 16:02.430
Listen, my husband and I were talking.

16:03.010 --> 16:08.960
We don't know anything about you 
or whoever brought you to us.

16:08.960 --> 16:14.500
But if... if you've got nowhere else to go,

16:14.790 --> 16:16.950
you're welcome to stay here.

16:17.470 --> 16:19.000
<i>Somewhere to go?</i>

16:20.510 --> 16:24.450
<i>I mustn't think about it. 
I can't live in that kingdom.</i>

16:25.030 --> 16:29.810
<i>Even if I make my way back, 
I'll just worry the king again.</i>

16:32.040 --> 16:35.640
Well, you don't have to make 
up your mind on the spot.

16:36.290 --> 16:38.180
Come on. Time for a breather.

16:38.570 --> 16:39.590
Right.

16:39.590 --> 16:41.540
<i>I need to keep moving forward.</i>

16:43.260 --> 16:46.890
A new girl at the clinic 
on the edge of town?

16:47.180 --> 16:50.770
I hear she was brought in for a 
sudden bout of miasma poisoning.

16:51.150 --> 16:54.150
But rumor has it she's from 
Noel Village, up north.

16:54.440 --> 16:59.900
Noel? Aren't they the ones 
who just sent a sacrifice?

17:01.330 --> 17:04.380
Hello! I'm here for the usual herbs and—

17:05.280 --> 17:08.340
H-Here! Take that and get out of here!

17:08.340 --> 17:10.740
Huh? But I haven't paid for—

17:10.740 --> 17:11.680
Just go!

17:16.580 --> 17:17.730
What's wrong?

17:17.730 --> 17:20.420
The townspeople seem different.

17:46.750 --> 17:48.250
Sir! Ma'am!

17:48.610 --> 17:50.870
Would you please leave, Sariphi?

17:51.690 --> 17:58.510
The whole town's whispering that you're 
a sacrifice escaped from the beast realm.

17:58.820 --> 18:02.180
They worry the king of beasts 
will come after you.

18:02.180 --> 18:05.700
That he'll raze the town for taking you in.

18:06.920 --> 18:10.030
You're right as rain now, aren't you?

18:10.490 --> 18:13.870
So please, just go somewhere else.

18:19.420 --> 18:21.820
<i>I've got nowhere to go again.</i>

18:23.030 --> 18:26.150
<i>But I guess that's nothing new.</i>

18:26.400 --> 18:28.580
...the king of beasts will come after you.

18:29.720 --> 18:31.630
<i>If only he would.</i>

18:32.470 --> 18:35.700
<i>But I'll be fine.</i>

18:37.320 --> 18:40.290
<i>Because no matter what happens to me,</i>

18:41.300 --> 18:43.400
<i>His Majesty will still be there.</i>

18:47.720 --> 18:50.650
<i>I... won't be fine.</i>

18:51.390 --> 18:54.380
<i>I can't go back to life without him.</i>

19:04.880 --> 19:07.650
I've been looking for you, Sariphi.

19:11.880 --> 19:15.030
Wh-What are you doing here, Your Majesty?

19:15.030 --> 19:17.060
And in human form, no less!

19:17.350 --> 19:23.280
In the human realm, free of miasma, 
I lose my beastly form and magical power.

19:23.280 --> 19:26.010
That made tracking you down a challenge.

19:26.250 --> 19:27.600
Tracking me?

19:28.250 --> 19:30.500
But I thought you left me behind.

19:31.250 --> 19:35.200
What are you talking about? 
I left you a letter.

19:35.610 --> 19:39.860
B-But I can't read beast writing yet.

19:41.400 --> 19:44.200
Wh-What did it say?

19:46.540 --> 19:50.160
I penned a promise to come back for you.

19:53.170 --> 19:54.640
Give me your hand.

19:54.640 --> 19:55.870
What's that?

19:56.350 --> 20:01.910
Ambrosia fruit purifies miasma. 
I used my magic to crystallize it.

20:02.500 --> 20:08.550
The fruit is a rarity in Ozmargo, 
so it took me some time to acquire.

20:09.150 --> 20:11.070
If you wear this at all times,

20:11.490 --> 20:15.640
the miasma will be purified 
as soon as it enters your body.

20:19.530 --> 20:26.010
Then... I can stay with you, sire? Leo?

20:28.940 --> 20:29.920
Fool.

20:31.730 --> 20:33.880
Don't ask the obvious.

20:33.880 --> 20:36.880
You are my queen.

20:42.000 --> 20:43.380
Sari!

20:43.380 --> 20:45.190
Welcome back!

20:45.190 --> 20:46.420
Back!

20:46.420 --> 20:48.850
It's good to be home, Cy, Clops!

20:49.200 --> 20:51.410
You're not sick anymore?

20:51.410 --> 20:53.330
Nope. I've never been better!

20:53.330 --> 20:55.200
Thank goodness!

20:55.200 --> 20:57.120
Good! Good!

20:56.310 --> 20:57.620
Thanks, you two!

20:58.180 --> 20:59.320
Listen, sire.

20:59.580 --> 21:03.970
I want to learn more about 
this land. About Ozmargo.

21:04.390 --> 21:08.590
I want to see its people with my own eyes.

21:09.120 --> 21:13.370
That may not be easy for a human like you.

21:14.430 --> 21:19.180
I'll be fine. It's the land I'm 
going to live in with you, sire.

21:19.180 --> 21:21.820
And I have this now.

21:22.810 --> 21:27.320
If you use that ring and give 
your body time to adjust,

21:27.320 --> 21:30.860
even a human should slowly develop 
an immunity to the miasma.

21:31.480 --> 21:34.630
Once that happens, 
you can remove that thing.

21:34.630 --> 21:36.760
Tolerate the inconvenience until—

21:36.760 --> 21:37.810
Sire,

21:38.470 --> 21:44.520
do you know what putting a ring on your 
left ring finger means in human lands?

21:47.460 --> 21:48.600
Well, you see,

21:49.690 --> 21:53.900
it's a token of a promise 
to stay together forever.

23:25.930 --> 23:27.990
Curse you, human wench!

23:27.990 --> 23:30.330
You leave me no choice but to summon 
princesses from far and wide!

23:30.330 --> 23:32.410
Once of <i>them</i> will be chosen 
as our formal queen to—

23:32.410 --> 23:33.430
Princesses?!

23:33.430 --> 23:36.320
